### ==========================================
### AUTHENTICATION & REGISTRATION ENDPOINTS (PUBLIC)
### ==========================================

### A1. Register a USER Account
POST http://localhost:8082/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alex User",
  "email": "alex@example.com",
  "password": "mySecurePassword123",
  "role": "USER"
}

### A2. Register an ADMIN Account
POST http://localhost:8082/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rio Admin",
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "adminPassword123",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### A3. Login as USER (Get your USER token here)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alex@example.com",
  "password": "mySecurePassword123"
}

### A4. Login as ADMIN (Get your ADMIN token here)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "adminPassword123"
}


### Test Register (Without role)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alex User",
  "email": "alex_test@example.com",
  "password": "mySecurePassword123"
}

### ==========================================
### TICKET API SECURITY TESTS
### ==========================================

### 1. GET /api/health (Should be Public -> 200 OK)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/health


### 2. GET /api/tickets WITHOUT Token (Should return 401 Unauthorized)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/tickets


### 3. GET /api/tickets WITH USER Token (Should return 200 OK)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 4. GET /api/tickets/{id} WITH USER Token (Should return 200 OK)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/tickets/6a51ed2b837a33b12a8318fe
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 5. POST /api/tickets WITH USER Token (Should return 403 Forbidden)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "title": "Broken Screen",
  "description": "The monitor in lab 3 is flashing green."
}


### 6. POST /api/tickets WITH ADMIN Token (Should return 201 Created)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "title": "Server Outage",
  "description": "Production database is not responding to connections.",
  "category": "Database",
  "priority": "Critical",
  "status": "Open",
  "createdBy": "Alex Admin"
}